// Workspace for local development across skyl's four modules.
//
// It exists so that a change spanning the library and an adapter builds without
// each module needing a `replace` pointing at a sibling directory. That matters
// because a `replace` is ignored by anyone whose main module is their own — so
// a published module carrying one still resolves its `require` line from the
// proxy, and a wrong `require` is invisible until someone outside this
// repository tries to install it. A workspace cannot make that mistake: Go
// never consults go.work when skyl is a dependency.
//
// CI therefore builds each module with GOWORK=off, which is the only way to
// check that every module resolves on its own. See RELEASING.md.
//
// The directive is 1.25 rather than the root module's 1.22 because a workspace
// must be at least as new as every member: the two adapter modules are pinned
// to 1.24 by the Anthropic SDK, and otel/ to 1.25 by the OpenTelemetry SDK.
// Only contributors pay that — CI builds every module with GOWORK=off, and a
// consumer of the library never sees this file.
go 1.25.0

use (
	.
	./gateway
	./otel
	./provider/anthropic
)
